================ 4. THE CLAIM: as the owner, with NO identity set, courier reads nothing ================

--- SQL ---
set role rls_probe_owner;
select count(*) from idempotency_keys;
--- output ---
0
PASS: the owner reads 0 of 2 rows — the boundary is LIVE on the owner path

--- SQL ---
set role rls_probe_owner;
select count(*) from notification_preferences;
--- output ---
0
PASS: the owner reads 0 of 2 rows — the boundary is LIVE on the owner path

--- SQL ---
set role rls_probe_owner;
select count(*) from webhook_endpoints;
--- output ---
0
PASS: the owner reads 0 of 2 rows — the boundary is LIVE on the owner path

================ 5. WHY NOBODY NOTICED: the same read as a SUPERUSER ================
--- SQL: select count(*) from idempotency_keys;   (as postgres)
--- output: 2
PASS: the superuser reads all 2 — which is why 219 green tests did not see this

================ 6. AND WITH begin_account/1, the owner reads its own account ================
--- SQL ---
set role rls_probe_owner;
select cafaye.begin_account('11111111-1111-4111-8111-111111111111');
select count(*) from idempotency_keys;
--- output ---

1
PASS: with an identity the owner reads its own row (1, not 2)

